+{"q": 75, "question": "Who is the most likely murderer?", "narrative": "In the cramped confines of an airplane mid-flight, Zoe was slain using a simple bottle of bleach, propelling Detective Winston into a sky-high murder mystery involving two main suspects: Russell and Alice.\n\nAs detective Winston stared at the boarded up airplane on the tarmac, his mind churned over the limited evidence he had at his disposal. Zoe, the cheerful flight stewardess was the victim, and he was about to interview one of the contentious suspects - a sailor by trade, a man named Russell. Detective Winston had seen him earlier that day. He was watching from a distance as Russell, with animal carcasses in tow, disappeared into his home. Winston didn't believe he had ever come across a more unique assortment of characters in any of his previous investigations. He sighed and decided it was time to meet with Russell, his main course of inquiry for the day.\n\nMaking his way to the docking area in the early morning light, he spotted a weathered sailor hunching over a bucket filled with cleaning supplies on his trawler. Bleach was prominent among them, a bottle of it sitting half used on the washed deck. As Winston approached, Russell began to explain how he had unintentionally injured himself in the past while cleaning his boat with the very same bleach. Despite the painful memory, it seemed he was determined to keep his ship sparking and sanitary as per his sailor training.\n\nDuring their conversation, Russell mentioned his aesthetics and love for taxidermy, a skill he had picked up during one of his various trips abroad, in particular, a trip to Norway. He explained how he always tried to learn something new from every country he visited, and Norway taught him taxidermy. \"And then there's my taxidermy workshop at home, in the basement,\" Russell revealed, \"...probably filled with dust bunnies now.\" He even told Winston about several animal carcasses he planned to work with later that evening in his basement workshop.\n\nFeeling he had gained his trust, Winston eased into the events which transpired in the airplane, \"You boarded the flight with Zoe, correct?\" Russell nodded, wrinkling his already weather-worn face. He began to retell his version of events. Winston noted that Russell started with how he found himself sitting next to Zoe on the airplane, further deepening their connection. From shared cab glasses to a friendly conversation which culminated in Russell offering Zoe a drink during the flight, the events were building up to an intricate narrative. Winston stored away these significant details which included their seating arrangement on the flight, to review later.\n\nAs the day wore on, Winston decided to wrap up his inquiry. Confirming with Russell his ticket receipt and presence on the same flight with Zoe, he felt he was making progress. An observing officer had provided his statement of seeing Russell board the same plane as Zoe. This was slowly shaping up into a complex murder mystery involving a sailor, bleach, taxidermy, and air travel. Winston ended his day at a local bar, quietly replaying the events of the day, piecing together this unique puzzle to get closer to the truth.\n\nThe piercing glare of Detective Winston enveloped the flamboyant spiritual guru Alice, as she walked towards him under the high terminal ceilings of the airport. Clad in flowing robes with bottles of various shapes and sizes dangling from her belt, she confidently greeted him. \n\n\"Detective Winston, I was expecting you. After all, one doesn't have to be a spiritual guru to know that after what happened, the police would want answers.\"\n\nWinston viewed her flamboyant getup briefly and caught sight of the wide variety of bottles she lugged around. Among them were the weirdly familiar-looking bleach bottles.\n\nAlice's past as a flight attendant was no secret. Through that career, she also formed a close bond with Zoe. They recently boarded a plane to